### AP-004: PII/PHI in Telemetry Attributes

**Description:** Including member IDs, patient names, SSNs, diagnosis codes, or any other regulated data in span attributes, metric labels, or log fields.

**Example of the anti-pattern:**
```csharp
// BAD: member ID and diagnosis code in span attributes
activity?.SetTag("member.id", request.MemberId);
activity?.SetTag("diagnosis.code", request.DiagnosisCode);
```

**Why it is harmful:** Telemetry backends are not HIPAA-compliant data stores by default. Introducing PHI into telemetry streams creates uncontrolled data flows outside the governed healthcare data environment, expanding audit scope and creating compliance risk.

**Correct approach:** Record the presence of a value, not the value itself. For claim IDs, use a hashed/tokenized form (see Section 3.5.1):
```csharp
// GOOD: presence/type indicators for PHI; hashed token for claim correlation
activity?.SetTag("gainwell.member.id_present", true);
activity?.SetTag("gainwell.claim.type", request.ClaimType);       // type, not content
activity?.SetTag("gainwell.claim.id_hash",                        // truncated hash for correlation
    Convert.ToHexString(
        SHA256.HashData(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(request.ClaimId))
    )[..16].ToLowerInvariant());
```

