### AP-006: Missing Exception Scrubbing

**Description:** Recording exception objects directly on spans without first sanitizing the exception message, which may contain query strings, serialized objects, or formatted strings that include PII/PHI.

**Example of the anti-pattern:**
```java
// BAD: exception message may include SQL query with row data or request body
span.recordException(e);
```

**Why it is harmful:** Exception messages frequently include contextual information such as SQL query parameters, HTTP request bodies, or formatted strings that contain PII/PHI. Recording raw exceptions passes this data to telemetry backends.

**Correct approach:**
```java
// GOOD: record exception type and a safe summary only
span.setStatus(StatusCode.ERROR, "Database operation failed");
span.setAttribute("exception.type", e.getClass().getName());
// Do NOT call span.recordException(e) if the exception may contain regulated data
```

